    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch02-07: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.63";
    dc:description "Biomechanical feasibility can be estimated with public scans and comparative traits, especially for the man-sized prediction. The categorical historical claims remain sensitive to uncertain soft tissues and what counts as ordinary anatomy.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Reconstruct body mass, wing area, muscle capacity and required flight power for ostrich, moa and comparably large flying birds, then test whether required power exceeds physiologically plausible muscle output under ordinary avian anatomy. A feasible positive power margin would refute physiological impossibility.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Extant ratites' reduced wings reflect evolutionary history as well as size.", "Moa soft tissue and wing anatomy require uncertain reconstruction.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.78"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch02-07--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch02-07--gpt--dataset-2>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.633"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch02-07--gpt--dataset-1> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/EvidenceItem>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Candidate dataset: MorphoSource";
    dc:description "3D skeletal scans of living and fossil birds for anatomical reconstruction.";
